# Phase 2: Data Preprocessing

## Objective

The objective of this phase is to prepare the cleaned dataset for machine learning by transforming and organizing the data into a suitable format.

---

## Encoding Categorical Data

Categorical features such as Gender were converted into numerical format using encoding techniques. This step is necessary because machine learning models can only work with numerical data.

---

## Data Transformation

The dataset already contained numerical values for Final_Grade, so no mapping was required. A new feature called Result was created based on Final_Grade to classify students as pass or fail.

---

## Feature Selection

Irrelevant features such as Student_ID and Student_Name were removed. Feature importance was analyzed using correlation, and only useful features were retained for model training.

---

## Normalization / Standardization

Data scaling was applied to ensure all features are on a similar scale. Standardization was used to transform the data so that it has a mean of 0 and a standard deviation of 1. This improves model performance and stability.

---

## Final Output

After preprocessing, the dataset was:

* Clean and free from inconsistencies
* Converted into numerical format
* Scaled and ready for model training

---

## Conclusion of Phase 2

This phase ensured that the dataset is properly prepared for machine learning. Proper preprocessing helps improve model accuracy and prevents errors during training.
